# The repository is written on Windows and deployed to Linux, and the
# deploy travels as `git archive`, so whatever git stores is what bash on
# the far end executes. A shell script checked out with CRLF fails there
# on its first line with a message about '\r' that names no useful cause.
#
# Only the files that are executed or parsed by the server are pinned.
# Everything else keeps git's own default, so nobody's editor fights this.
*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
